1
00:00:14,381 --> 00:00:17,083
Your phone's ringing.

2
00:00:21,521 --> 00:00:22,355
Gosh.

3
00:00:24,290 --> 00:00:25,759
Mine?

4
00:00:32,766 --> 00:00:34,000
It's mine.

5
00:00:34,768 --> 00:00:36,036
Michiko. Let's go.

6
00:00:37,037 --> 00:00:38,705
No way.

7
00:00:38,772 --> 00:00:41,074
AKIRA KANBARA
HEAD OF KANBARA DOCTOR AGENCY

8
00:00:41,608 --> 00:00:42,876
What's wrong, Michiko?

9
00:00:44,778 --> 00:00:46,446
Akira!

10
00:00:46,913 --> 00:00:48,148
Akira!

11
00:00:48,214 --> 00:00:49,149
Akira!

12
00:00:50,450 --> 00:00:51,851
Let me borrow money.

13
00:00:55,588 --> 00:00:57,757
Michiko, how shameless!

14
00:00:59,192 --> 00:01:00,226
Stop it.

15
00:01:00,293 --> 00:01:02,796
Come on, Akira.

16
00:01:02,862 --> 00:01:05,298
Lend me 30,000 yen.

17
00:01:05,365 --> 00:01:07,067
For what?

18
00:01:07,133 --> 00:01:09,369
It's a secret.

19
00:01:09,969 --> 00:01:10,937
For a guy?

20
00:01:13,973 --> 00:01:14,808
Not telling.

21
00:01:15,175 --> 00:01:17,043
Want money? Do surgery.

22
00:01:17,477 --> 00:01:18,478
I want it now.

23
00:01:18,545 --> 00:01:21,014
Let me borrow in advance. Please.

24
00:01:21,448 --> 00:01:23,783
You're not a kid.

25
00:01:23,850 --> 00:01:27,087
<i>This is the story of</i>
<i>a lone wolf woman doctor.</i>

26
00:01:29,222 --> 00:01:32,659
There might be some trouble.

27
00:01:34,327 --> 00:01:35,328
What do you mean?

28
00:01:37,697 --> 00:01:39,833
A man named Takashi Rokko

29
00:01:41,134 --> 00:01:43,970
will go to your hospital for a checkup.

30
00:01:46,606 --> 00:01:49,542
- Yes.
- Regardless of the results...

31
00:01:49,609 --> 00:01:51,177
It would be helpful

32
00:01:52,545 --> 00:01:56,116
if you could look after him for a while.

33
00:01:56,916 --> 00:01:59,619
A while?

34
00:02:02,489 --> 00:02:06,793
Accepting the good and the bad
is part of politics.

35
00:02:10,897 --> 00:02:12,699
If you can overcome this,

36
00:02:14,167 --> 00:02:19,139
the Ministry of Health, Labour and Welfare

37
00:02:19,539 --> 00:02:21,908
will support your
Japan Healthcare Organization idea.

38
00:02:25,178 --> 00:02:29,949
The authority held by the
ministries should be concentrated.

39
00:02:30,016 --> 00:02:34,320
Creating a new organization
is an urgent matter.

40
00:02:37,757 --> 00:02:40,593
I look forward to hearing good news.

41
00:02:48,234 --> 00:02:49,469
<i>In 2014,</i>

42
00:02:49,936 --> 00:02:52,839
<i>the once sacrosanct university</i>
<i>medical system was in crisis.</i>

43
00:02:58,511 --> 00:03:00,246
- Thanks.
- Good luck, sir.

44
00:03:01,347 --> 00:03:03,483
<i>The system on which lives depend</i>

45
00:03:04,017 --> 00:03:07,287
<i>had strayed away from what it should be.</i>

46
00:03:12,792 --> 00:03:17,497
Unified Director Ebina of Strategically
Integrated Surgical Department

47
00:03:17,564 --> 00:03:19,365
will now make his rounds.

48
00:03:22,068 --> 00:03:25,905
I heard the term "unified."

49
00:03:25,972 --> 00:03:26,806
Yes,

50
00:03:26,873 --> 00:03:29,609
the department's "Unified Director."

51
00:03:29,676 --> 00:03:32,212
<i>However, despite these conditions,</i>

52
00:03:32,545 --> 00:03:36,549
<i>Japan announced to export</i>
<i>the latest medical services</i>

53
00:03:36,616 --> 00:03:39,319
<i>as a growth strategy.</i>

54
00:03:39,886 --> 00:03:44,290
<i>The medical industry</i>
<i>had reverted to the law of the jungle.</i>

55
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:48,928
Get in line.

56
00:03:50,463 --> 00:03:51,831
- Yes, sir.
- No.

57
00:03:54,334 --> 00:03:55,401
- Yes, sir.
- Louder.

58
00:03:56,436 --> 00:03:57,303
Yes, sir!

59
00:04:05,545 --> 00:04:07,914
It's a unification of the empire.

60
00:04:08,514 --> 00:04:11,751
- You did it, Dr. Ebina.
- Call me Unified Director.

61
00:04:24,831 --> 00:04:26,966
HIROMI JONOUCHI, ANESTHESIOLOGIST

62
00:04:31,404 --> 00:04:32,238
Rokko?

63
00:04:33,006 --> 00:04:34,340
Jonouchi.

64
00:04:36,576 --> 00:04:40,847
<i>Doctors who don't belong to</i>
<i>any medical offices appeared.</i>

65
00:04:40,913 --> 00:04:44,684
<i>Freelance doctors, in other words,</i>
<i>maverick doctors.</i>

66
00:04:45,752 --> 00:04:47,020
Get in line.

67
00:04:47,086 --> 00:04:48,021
I decline.

68
00:04:52,692 --> 00:04:53,993
Can I borrow 30,000 yen?

69
00:04:54,794 --> 00:04:55,762
I'll pay back double.

70
00:04:56,929 --> 00:04:57,764
Dr. Ebina.

71
00:04:58,765 --> 00:05:01,601
The patient you will
be in charge of is here.

72
00:05:03,202 --> 00:05:05,004
Oh, the rich IT guy here for a checkup.

73
00:05:05,071 --> 00:05:06,239
He's in his room.

74
00:05:06,306 --> 00:05:07,774
A simple checkup

75
00:05:07,840 --> 00:05:10,443
isn't the job of the Unified Director.

76
00:05:12,045 --> 00:05:12,879
Who's free?

77
00:05:16,349 --> 00:05:18,151
Daimon. You're in charge.

78
00:05:18,985 --> 00:05:20,486
This is an order.

79
00:05:20,553 --> 00:05:21,621
You cannot refuse.

80
00:05:21,688 --> 00:05:23,423
It's just a checkup.

81
00:05:26,893 --> 00:05:27,894
You do it.

82
00:05:29,128 --> 00:05:30,363
That's a great idea.

83
00:05:30,930 --> 00:05:33,166
A refugee of the West and the part-timer.

84
00:05:34,867 --> 00:05:36,769
The two of you make a whole.

85
00:05:37,270 --> 00:05:38,204
Fine.

86
00:05:38,271 --> 00:05:40,840
Achi, you be Daimon's assistant.

87
00:05:41,574 --> 00:05:42,642
Assistant?

88
00:05:47,714 --> 00:05:49,649
He crushed his surviving pride.

89
00:05:50,283 --> 00:05:53,519
Pity brings disaster. It must be done.

90
00:05:59,892 --> 00:06:02,095
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

91
00:06:02,829 --> 00:06:06,499
<i>She despises groups, authority</i>
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

92
00:06:06,566 --> 00:06:11,137
<i>Her only weapons are her license</i>
<i>and the skills she has earned.</i>

93
00:06:12,271 --> 00:06:13,706
Michiko Daimon, yes?

94
00:06:14,407 --> 00:06:15,508
What?

95
00:06:15,575 --> 00:06:18,177
I'm Ichikawa from the Prosecutor's Office.

96
00:06:18,244 --> 00:06:20,546
I'm Uehara, his assistant.

97
00:06:21,981 --> 00:06:23,149
Prosecutor?

98
00:06:23,983 --> 00:06:27,086
May we speak with you?

99
00:06:30,022 --> 00:06:32,158
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

100
00:06:33,426 --> 00:06:36,796
<i>Also known as Doctor-X.</i>

101
00:07:05,825 --> 00:07:07,260
30ml of Pentazocine.

102
00:07:07,326 --> 00:07:08,194
Yes.

103
00:07:10,630 --> 00:07:12,899
You went to school with Dr. Jonouchi?

104
00:07:13,299 --> 00:07:14,200
High school.

105
00:07:14,767 --> 00:07:17,336
Jonouchi was my first love.

106
00:07:17,403 --> 00:07:20,006
You said that to every girl.

107
00:07:20,072 --> 00:07:21,974
Oh, you knew.

108
00:07:22,942 --> 00:07:25,511
No wonder no one took me seriously.

109
00:07:25,578 --> 00:07:28,247
That's how he is.

110
00:07:28,314 --> 00:07:29,148
Always babbling.

111
00:07:29,549 --> 00:07:30,516
No.

112
00:07:31,484 --> 00:07:33,219
I need your permission.

113
00:07:33,286 --> 00:07:35,154
I said no.

114
00:07:35,555 --> 00:07:36,389
Who's this?

115
00:07:36,456 --> 00:07:38,024
Mr. Takashi Rokko?

116
00:07:39,091 --> 00:07:41,027
I'm from the Prosecutor's Office.

117
00:07:42,628 --> 00:07:45,031
Could I speak to you

118
00:07:45,097 --> 00:07:46,466
about Minister Oizumi?

119
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:48,534
I said no.

120
00:07:48,601 --> 00:07:49,569
Then allow us.

121
00:07:50,670 --> 00:07:52,205
It seems he can speak.

122
00:07:52,271 --> 00:07:54,040
Don't diagnose him.

123
00:07:54,106 --> 00:07:56,075
Would everyone please leave?

124
00:08:02,114 --> 00:08:03,683
- The pen light.
- Yes.

125
00:08:08,154 --> 00:08:09,222
Please leave.

126
00:08:10,723 --> 00:08:12,158
It's the doctor's order.

127
00:08:19,031 --> 00:08:20,132
Daimon...

128
00:08:20,833 --> 00:08:22,502
I don't like bossy people.

129
00:08:27,106 --> 00:08:28,708
Thanks. I'll give you a gift.

130
00:08:29,141 --> 00:08:30,376
Will you hand me that?

131
00:08:31,644 --> 00:08:32,545
This?

132
00:08:41,220 --> 00:08:43,022
What's the usual price?

133
00:08:47,960 --> 00:08:48,961
Just 3?

134
00:08:51,831 --> 00:08:53,432
- Here.
- Seriously?

135
00:08:53,499 --> 00:08:56,435
Rokko, that's not allowed.

136
00:08:57,403 --> 00:08:58,504
Daimon!

137
00:08:59,505 --> 00:09:00,806
I just need 30,000.

138
00:09:06,879 --> 00:09:08,648
I understand his condition.

139
00:09:10,383 --> 00:09:12,385
But he can still speak.

140
00:09:12,852 --> 00:09:15,755
You can speak to him.

141
00:09:16,122 --> 00:09:19,892
However, he's received
a large dose of painkillers.

142
00:09:19,959 --> 00:09:23,896
Could you say that
his mind is totally clear?

143
00:09:23,963 --> 00:09:26,999
A patient here for
a checkup has a brain tumor...

144
00:09:27,800 --> 00:09:31,070
We cannot help but have doubts.

145
00:09:31,137 --> 00:09:33,839
Are you saying this is a lie?

146
00:09:33,906 --> 00:09:36,676
He may be using
this hospital to hide himself.

147
00:09:37,543 --> 00:09:39,345
It's a possibility.

148
00:09:42,315 --> 00:09:46,953
The Prosecutor's Office will have to
get a second opinion about this.

149
00:09:48,354 --> 00:09:50,723
He has glioblastoma.

150
00:09:50,790 --> 00:09:52,491
Any doctor would say so.

151
00:09:53,893 --> 00:09:58,230
Cerebral edema too.
There's high intracranial pressure.

152
00:09:59,532 --> 00:10:01,934
It's a serious, malignant brain tumor.

153
00:10:02,602 --> 00:10:05,071
He'll die if he's not treated.

154
00:10:09,775 --> 00:10:12,545
I understand. We'll be leaving today.

155
00:10:13,446 --> 00:10:15,615
We'll be back, though.

156
00:10:15,681 --> 00:10:18,818
We have no intentions of refusing to help.

157
00:10:20,453 --> 00:10:21,354
Sorry.

158
00:10:32,865 --> 00:10:33,699
Excuse me.

159
00:10:35,401 --> 00:10:37,036
What's up with that patient?

160
00:10:37,803 --> 00:10:41,340
Dr. Daimon.
Do not pry into unnecessary matters.

161
00:10:42,675 --> 00:10:44,677
Is it an unbelievable secret?

162
00:10:45,478 --> 00:10:46,979
Dr. Daimon.

163
00:10:47,046 --> 00:10:51,817
I ask that you
focus on the treatment as usual.

164
00:10:52,852 --> 00:10:53,686
Yes.

165
00:10:55,388 --> 00:10:56,222
Here.

166
00:11:02,228 --> 00:11:03,195
Mr. Tendo.

167
00:11:04,497 --> 00:11:05,364
Well...

168
00:11:05,431 --> 00:11:08,300
I have no clue what's going on.

169
00:11:08,768 --> 00:11:10,736
But I will make sure

170
00:11:10,803 --> 00:11:15,975
Daimon doesn't nose around
and does her job. Please rest assured.

171
00:11:17,743 --> 00:11:19,078
Dr. Ebina.

172
00:11:19,145 --> 00:11:19,979
Yes.

173
00:11:22,948 --> 00:11:24,016
Why did you...

174
00:11:25,484 --> 00:11:30,022
have Dr. Daimon be the physician instead?

175
00:11:45,204 --> 00:11:47,840
This is really bad.

176
00:11:48,674 --> 00:11:53,312
Of all people, Demon's the physician
of such a problematic patient...

177
00:11:57,249 --> 00:11:58,084
3 days...

178
00:12:00,019 --> 00:12:02,054
Thinking I had a short reign?

179
00:12:03,789 --> 00:12:05,257
Trying to say

180
00:12:06,525 --> 00:12:09,161
I should be happy for being at the top...

181
00:12:10,396 --> 00:12:12,598
- even if it was for 3 days?
- No.

182
00:12:15,634 --> 00:12:16,802
Of course not.

183
00:12:20,039 --> 00:12:20,873
Then,

184
00:12:22,141 --> 00:12:23,676
I have a favor to ask you.

185
00:12:28,347 --> 00:12:32,384
Dr. Achi, it's about a patient
named Takashi Rokko.

186
00:12:32,918 --> 00:12:34,453
- Yes?
- From now on,

187
00:12:35,187 --> 00:12:37,890
please report everything about him to me.

188
00:12:38,724 --> 00:12:43,963
Do not let any information leak.
Treat this matter with the utmost secrecy.

189
00:12:45,698 --> 00:12:46,699
Secrecy?

190
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:48,868
Now...

191
00:12:50,102 --> 00:12:53,005
Please understand that
this is an order from Mr. Tendo.

192
00:12:54,340 --> 00:12:55,307
Is that alright?

193
00:12:56,942 --> 00:12:58,778
Yes, sir.

194
00:13:01,180 --> 00:13:02,548
Is Daimon here?

195
00:13:02,615 --> 00:13:03,749
You cannot enter.

196
00:13:03,816 --> 00:13:04,950
- Why?
- Please leave.

197
00:13:05,017 --> 00:13:06,619
- What?
- Get out!

198
00:13:07,853 --> 00:13:08,687
You should go too.

199
00:13:10,289 --> 00:13:12,525
- Daimon!
- Wait.

200
00:13:14,527 --> 00:13:15,461
Just come.

201
00:13:15,528 --> 00:13:16,896
What?

202
00:13:22,034 --> 00:13:23,435
What?

203
00:13:27,740 --> 00:13:30,042
Daimon, you need money, right?

204
00:13:34,747 --> 00:13:36,682
It's from Unified Director Ebina.

205
00:13:37,883 --> 00:13:39,018
30,000 yen.

206
00:13:39,552 --> 00:13:43,823
He wants you to let him be
the physician for that patient.

207
00:13:57,503 --> 00:13:58,470
Not enough.

208
00:13:59,939 --> 00:14:02,308
- 20,000?
- He bargained?

209
00:14:02,374 --> 00:14:03,442
Too bad.

210
00:14:05,044 --> 00:14:06,011
It really is.

211
00:14:06,078 --> 00:14:08,747
- What's his problem?
- I'm scared.

212
00:14:10,616 --> 00:14:12,418
So Rokko,

213
00:14:12,484 --> 00:14:14,520
what did you do

214
00:14:14,587 --> 00:14:15,855
to get prosecutors here?

215
00:14:16,255 --> 00:14:17,122
Well...

216
00:14:17,923 --> 00:14:19,225
I can't say.

217
00:14:21,694 --> 00:14:22,628
Money?

218
00:14:23,729 --> 00:14:25,030
I wonder.

219
00:14:25,698 --> 00:14:27,867
We all have secrets.

220
00:14:28,367 --> 00:14:31,337
I don't have any secrets.

221
00:14:31,403 --> 00:14:32,938
Don't lie.

222
00:14:33,505 --> 00:14:36,075
In senior year of high school, you...

223
00:14:37,376 --> 00:14:39,044
How do you know? Stop it.

224
00:14:41,614 --> 00:14:44,083
I bet our classmates are shocked.

225
00:14:45,084 --> 00:14:47,720
I had the worst grades in class,

226
00:14:48,320 --> 00:14:51,690
but I became the richest one.

227
00:14:52,558 --> 00:14:54,894
Yes, it's unbelievable.

228
00:14:56,328 --> 00:14:57,196
Money is great.

229
00:14:57,830 --> 00:14:59,365
Everyone looks at you.

230
00:15:00,266 --> 00:15:01,600
You can make them look too.

231
00:15:02,635 --> 00:15:03,502
Bragging?

232
00:15:04,670 --> 00:15:08,507
I'd buy new import cars
like they were colored pencils.

233
00:15:09,441 --> 00:15:13,545
And I'd get a new girl every time too.

234
00:15:14,780 --> 00:15:17,283
But I was so unpopular in school.

235
00:15:18,217 --> 00:15:20,286
What's great about girls
who look at you for money?

236
00:15:20,352 --> 00:15:21,186
"Money isn't everything."

237
00:15:23,322 --> 00:15:27,126
"There are things money can't buy."

238
00:15:29,461 --> 00:15:31,964
Some say that like they know,

239
00:15:32,031 --> 00:15:33,098
but they

240
00:15:33,933 --> 00:15:35,634
just look like jealous

241
00:15:35,701 --> 00:15:37,903
and useless pests.

242
00:15:39,538 --> 00:15:40,940
You mean me?

243
00:15:41,540 --> 00:15:42,408
Of course not.

244
00:15:43,876 --> 00:15:45,744
I realized that's what

245
00:15:46,278 --> 00:15:48,614
it takes to obtain money.

246
00:15:48,948 --> 00:15:50,349
You've changed, Rokko.

247
00:15:52,384 --> 00:15:54,320
That's how I succeeded.

248
00:15:57,589 --> 00:15:59,692
I came here saying it's a checkup,

249
00:16:00,359 --> 00:16:02,227
but I've been to a few hospitals.

250
00:16:05,397 --> 00:16:06,432
It was a mistake!

251
00:16:06,832 --> 00:16:10,469
I went to many hospitals,
saying "No, it's a misdiagnosis."

252
00:16:11,537 --> 00:16:12,471
I see.

253
00:16:13,272 --> 00:16:14,106
But...

254
00:16:15,674 --> 00:16:18,544
every hospital said the same thing.

255
00:16:23,248 --> 00:16:26,385
I don't have much time left, right?

256
00:16:28,520 --> 00:16:30,055
I'd say 6 months at this rate.

257
00:16:34,093 --> 00:16:35,194
You've always

258
00:16:36,128 --> 00:16:37,396
been blunt, Jonouchi.

259
00:16:41,967 --> 00:16:43,736
"There are things money can't buy."

260
00:16:45,971 --> 00:16:47,306
When I realized this,

261
00:16:49,508 --> 00:16:50,943
I only had 6 months to live.

262
00:16:58,784 --> 00:17:00,819
KANBARA DOCTOR AGENCY

263
00:17:03,555 --> 00:17:04,490
Bribery?

264
00:17:04,556 --> 00:17:07,993
Yes. If the Prosecutor's Office
is on the move,

265
00:17:08,794 --> 00:17:10,462
it must be a political scheme.

266
00:17:11,030 --> 00:17:13,365
He's a rich IT guy.

267
00:17:13,432 --> 00:17:15,134
I can smell the money.

268
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:17,669
Tons of cash must be involved.

269
00:17:17,736 --> 00:17:19,938
Yeah, this means 3 million.

270
00:17:20,005 --> 00:17:21,607
Don't know anything?

271
00:17:21,673 --> 00:17:23,275
You're his classmate.

272
00:17:23,342 --> 00:17:24,543
Reach!

273
00:17:24,610 --> 00:17:26,645
I know nothing.

274
00:17:26,712 --> 00:17:29,648
More importantly,
what are you going to do?

275
00:17:29,715 --> 00:17:32,217
- About what?
- The surgery. Reach!

276
00:17:32,651 --> 00:17:34,686
What can she do?

277
00:17:35,654 --> 00:17:38,724
The cerebral tissue's infiltrated.

278
00:17:38,791 --> 00:17:39,658
I can do it.

279
00:17:39,725 --> 00:17:40,859
Really?

280
00:17:40,926 --> 00:17:44,263
No way. Even you
can't remove the whole tumor.

281
00:17:44,329 --> 00:17:45,697
Why not try, Hiromi?

282
00:17:45,764 --> 00:17:47,499
The surgery?

283
00:17:47,566 --> 00:17:48,467
No.

284
00:17:48,534 --> 00:17:50,202
If he's dying soon,

285
00:17:50,269 --> 00:17:52,905
you can marry him to
inherit tons of money.

286
00:17:54,106 --> 00:17:55,941
How awful.

287
00:17:56,008 --> 00:17:57,443
You're evil.

288
00:18:01,780 --> 00:18:02,614
Wow!

289
00:18:05,984 --> 00:18:06,985
Could you play for me?

290
00:18:07,319 --> 00:18:09,054
Just for a bit.

291
00:18:11,924 --> 00:18:12,758
What's wrong?

292
00:18:12,825 --> 00:18:14,793
She's got a man.

293
00:18:14,860 --> 00:18:17,796
A no-good man who tries to get 30,000 yen.

294
00:18:18,197 --> 00:18:19,565
Seriously?

295
00:18:22,768 --> 00:18:23,869
What?

296
00:18:23,936 --> 00:18:25,204
Ron!

297
00:18:25,270 --> 00:18:26,105
8,000 points.

298
00:18:26,171 --> 00:18:28,540
- Me too.
- Seriously?

299
00:18:28,607 --> 00:18:29,808
Gosh!

300
00:18:31,276 --> 00:18:33,545
Michiko, sorry.

301
00:18:33,612 --> 00:18:35,514
They both got me.

302
00:18:36,715 --> 00:18:38,517
- Seriously?
- Yeah.

303
00:18:40,285 --> 00:18:41,553
Don't worry.

304
00:18:42,354 --> 00:18:43,222
It's fine.

305
00:18:51,396 --> 00:18:52,831
WEST

306
00:18:56,268 --> 00:18:57,336
Thanks.

307
00:18:59,004 --> 00:19:03,542
That's hard work. A complete removal
of the tumor is impossible.

308
00:19:04,076 --> 00:19:05,410
Demon, understand?

309
00:19:05,477 --> 00:19:08,847
If you try,
he'll lose his use of language.

310
00:19:08,914 --> 00:19:10,149
Be quiet.

311
00:20:02,901 --> 00:20:03,769
Yes?

312
00:20:08,507 --> 00:20:09,541
Some candy?

313
00:20:09,608 --> 00:20:10,609
CANDY

314
00:20:15,948 --> 00:20:17,616
I see.

315
00:20:25,691 --> 00:20:27,459
I'm counting on you, assistant.

316
00:20:31,396 --> 00:20:33,365
NATIONAL ADVANCED MEDICAL CENTER

317
00:20:40,906 --> 00:20:44,209
We will now begin
this week's preoperative conference.

318
00:20:45,711 --> 00:20:47,779
The first case is Takashi Rokko,

319
00:20:47,846 --> 00:20:49,481
a 35-year-old male.

320
00:20:49,548 --> 00:20:53,018
The diagnosis is glioblastoma.

321
00:20:53,085 --> 00:20:55,721
The surgeon is Dr. Daimon.

322
00:20:55,787 --> 00:20:58,090
The 1st assistant is Dr. Achi.

323
00:21:00,859 --> 00:21:03,829
I'm Achi. Let me explain.

324
00:21:05,497 --> 00:21:09,201
The left frontal lobe has
a 7cm tumor with extensive edema.

325
00:21:10,202 --> 00:21:12,471
It's near the Broca's area,

326
00:21:12,537 --> 00:21:14,306
and there may be infiltration.

327
00:21:14,773 --> 00:21:17,209
We will perform awake

328
00:21:17,276 --> 00:21:19,511
craniotomy glioblastoma resection

329
00:21:19,878 --> 00:21:21,780
to remove the whole tumor.

330
00:21:21,847 --> 00:21:24,616
Please speak about the risks.

331
00:21:24,683 --> 00:21:25,717
Yes.

332
00:21:25,784 --> 00:21:30,255
At worst, death during surgery from
a seizure or suffocation.

333
00:21:30,322 --> 00:21:33,158
Forcibly removing the tumor

334
00:21:33,225 --> 00:21:36,461
could make him paralyzed or aphasic.

335
00:21:36,895 --> 00:21:39,498
What if that happens?

336
00:21:39,564 --> 00:21:42,301
We're doing awake surgery
so it won't happen.

337
00:21:44,503 --> 00:21:45,470
Dr. Daimon.

338
00:21:46,805 --> 00:21:50,175
Are you planning to
remove the entire tumor?

339
00:21:50,842 --> 00:21:52,144
That's my plan.

340
00:22:02,054 --> 00:22:03,188
Daimon, wait.

341
00:22:05,057 --> 00:22:07,859
Even you think that's impossible, right?

342
00:22:08,493 --> 00:22:10,262
I won't know unless I try.

343
00:22:11,229 --> 00:22:12,964
The prosecution's after him.

344
00:22:14,933 --> 00:22:16,168
What if you fail?

345
00:22:17,302 --> 00:22:18,804
I never fail.

346
00:22:19,237 --> 00:22:20,272
How?

347
00:22:22,941 --> 00:22:24,176
It's a secret.

348
00:22:30,115 --> 00:22:31,983
Wake up during surgery?

349
00:22:32,918 --> 00:22:34,219
- Me?
- Yes.

350
00:22:34,286 --> 00:22:36,321
You'll come off the anesthetics,

351
00:22:36,388 --> 00:22:38,790
and speak during surgery.

352
00:22:39,358 --> 00:22:42,594
It's to check that we're
not damaging your brain.

353
00:22:43,061 --> 00:22:44,262
I see.

354
00:22:44,329 --> 00:22:46,531
Don't worry.

355
00:22:46,598 --> 00:22:49,334
She may look like this,
but she's the best here.

356
00:22:49,401 --> 00:22:51,670
- Looks aren't important.
- Sorry.

357
00:22:51,737 --> 00:22:53,438
It's a risky operation, right?

358
00:22:54,773 --> 00:22:55,674
Yeah.

359
00:22:55,741 --> 00:22:57,976
You're a part-timer, after all.

360
00:22:58,377 --> 00:22:59,411
I'm a freelancer.

361
00:23:01,480 --> 00:23:02,481
I'm out of luck.

362
00:23:03,248 --> 00:23:05,851
This is what I get for the end.

363
00:23:10,155 --> 00:23:13,558
I have a secret that I can't speak of.

364
00:23:15,026 --> 00:23:16,862
A secret that, if revealed,

365
00:23:18,130 --> 00:23:23,301
will greatly damage
some people and myself.

366
00:23:25,470 --> 00:23:29,975
There are people who
can't wait for me to die.

367
00:23:31,176 --> 00:23:32,310
What are you talking about?

368
00:23:33,678 --> 00:23:34,513
Jonouchi.

369
00:23:35,947 --> 00:23:38,917
If I take all those at once,

370
00:23:39,584 --> 00:23:41,520
- can I die?
- Cut it out!

371
00:23:42,687 --> 00:23:45,357
I don't know what you're hiding,

372
00:23:45,991 --> 00:23:48,727
but if you broke the law, then say it.

373
00:23:49,795 --> 00:23:51,530
Trying to die and escape?

374
00:23:53,265 --> 00:23:54,766
You're sick.

375
00:23:59,738 --> 00:24:01,940
I don't care about that stuff.

376
00:24:03,442 --> 00:24:05,577
Just don't die before surgery.

377
00:24:06,978 --> 00:24:08,780
I can't operate if you're dead.

378
00:24:09,548 --> 00:24:10,682
Bye.

379
00:24:31,670 --> 00:24:32,838
Postpone it?

380
00:24:32,904 --> 00:24:35,607
If an accident were to
occur during surgery,

381
00:24:36,341 --> 00:24:38,643
we lose the patient's testimony.

382
00:24:38,710 --> 00:24:42,380
We must avoid that no matter what.

383
00:24:42,447 --> 00:24:44,483
The patient needs urgent care.

384
00:24:45,150 --> 00:24:47,252
The tumor is worsening by the day.

385
00:24:48,620 --> 00:24:51,089
- We refuse.
- Mr. Tendo.

386
00:24:52,157 --> 00:24:54,826
You and Minister Oizumi were promoting

387
00:24:55,694 --> 00:25:00,899
the establishment of a medical service
network infrastructure in Southeast Asia.

388
00:25:01,933 --> 00:25:02,868
And?

389
00:25:02,934 --> 00:25:04,936
I heard a Japanese IT corporation

390
00:25:05,003 --> 00:25:10,675
will give a great amount
of money to those involved.

391
00:25:12,711 --> 00:25:15,881
You're not involved, are you?

392
00:25:21,419 --> 00:25:23,121
I believe you should

393
00:25:23,188 --> 00:25:25,690
investigate thoroughly

394
00:25:26,291 --> 00:25:29,327
before mentioning such things.

395
00:25:29,394 --> 00:25:30,762
Is that a threat?

396
00:25:30,829 --> 00:25:31,663
How rude!

397
00:25:33,532 --> 00:25:35,367
That is not appropriate.

398
00:25:38,537 --> 00:25:41,106
If you're that curious,

399
00:25:42,641 --> 00:25:45,510
why don't you attend the operation?

400
00:25:46,912 --> 00:25:48,079
What?

401
00:25:48,146 --> 00:25:50,982
You can witness our principle

402
00:25:51,049 --> 00:25:53,552
of putting one's life as the top priority.

403
00:26:14,506 --> 00:26:15,674
IN SURGERY

404
00:26:21,146 --> 00:26:24,449
We will now begin the awake craniotomy.

405
00:26:24,516 --> 00:26:26,017
- Please begin.
- Please.

406
00:26:26,084 --> 00:26:27,552
Let's begin.

407
00:26:27,619 --> 00:26:30,555
Blood pressure 100s, pulse 80s and sinus.

408
00:26:31,189 --> 00:26:32,123
- Scalpel.
- Yes.

409
00:26:45,303 --> 00:26:46,471
- Scalp clip.
- Yes.

410
00:26:46,938 --> 00:26:47,906
- Suction.
- Yes.

411
00:27:03,388 --> 00:27:04,255
Right this way.

412
00:27:30,615 --> 00:27:31,850
- Metzenbaum.
- Yes.

413
00:27:43,261 --> 00:27:44,629
Brain exposed.

414
00:27:45,130 --> 00:27:46,831
- Wake him up.
- Yes.

415
00:27:47,432 --> 00:27:49,234
Stopping the propofol.

416
00:27:52,170 --> 00:27:53,838
- Open the drapes.
- Yes.

417
00:27:53,905 --> 00:27:55,073
- Get the microscope.
- Yes.

418
00:27:56,041 --> 00:27:57,142
He'll wake up now.

419
00:28:24,402 --> 00:28:25,270
Good morning.

420
00:28:28,440 --> 00:28:32,110
- Are you operating on me?
- Yes.

421
00:28:34,479 --> 00:28:35,980
Unbelievable.

422
00:28:37,415 --> 00:28:38,717
Let's begin.

423
00:28:38,783 --> 00:28:40,218
- Stimulation probe.
- Yes.

424
00:28:41,486 --> 00:28:43,455
- 2 milliamperes.
- Yes.

425
00:28:44,089 --> 00:28:45,523
First, motor area.

426
00:28:46,491 --> 00:28:50,095
Rokko, open and close your right hand.

427
00:29:03,875 --> 00:29:04,976
Stable.

428
00:29:05,043 --> 00:29:06,211
You can stop, Rokko.

429
00:29:06,778 --> 00:29:08,913
- Okay. Bipolar.
- Yes.

430
00:29:08,980 --> 00:29:10,582
- Saline.
- Yes.

431
00:29:17,756 --> 00:29:19,023
- Micro scissors.
- Yes.

432
00:29:21,593 --> 00:29:23,928
SURGERY TIME

433
00:29:23,995 --> 00:29:25,096
Next, speech area.

434
00:29:25,497 --> 00:29:27,499
- Lower to 1 milliampere.
- Yes.

435
00:29:27,565 --> 00:29:29,701
Say your name.

436
00:29:31,436 --> 00:29:35,006
Takashi Rokko...

437
00:29:35,073 --> 00:29:36,074
Your age?

438
00:29:38,143 --> 00:29:39,911
We're classmates.

439
00:29:39,978 --> 00:29:41,513
Just answer me.

440
00:29:42,714 --> 00:29:44,783
35

441
00:29:45,350 --> 00:29:46,217
Stable.

442
00:29:46,284 --> 00:29:47,118
Yes.

443
00:29:47,552 --> 00:29:49,788
Looks good.

444
00:29:49,854 --> 00:29:50,755
Keep asking him.

445
00:29:50,822 --> 00:29:53,057
Rokko, when's your birthday?

446
00:29:54,826 --> 00:29:59,230
1979...

447
00:30:02,634 --> 00:30:03,701
900...

448
00:30:05,103 --> 00:30:05,937
Can't speak?

449
00:30:13,711 --> 00:30:15,814
Can you hear me?

450
00:30:21,553 --> 00:30:23,454
I can't go on.

451
00:30:24,355 --> 00:30:26,257
The tumor will remain.

452
00:30:26,658 --> 00:30:28,326
Even you can't do it?

453
00:30:29,928 --> 00:30:30,762
No.

454
00:30:38,803 --> 00:30:40,605
The tumor will remain.

455
00:30:41,039 --> 00:30:42,707
Even you can't do it?

456
00:30:44,342 --> 00:30:45,543
No.

457
00:30:50,315 --> 00:30:51,783
I knew it.

458
00:30:53,218 --> 00:30:55,553
Even she can't do it.

459
00:30:55,620 --> 00:30:58,756
Michiko Daimon loses.

460
00:31:06,331 --> 00:31:10,468
I'm going to die like this.

461
00:31:10,535 --> 00:31:12,103
I won't let you die.

462
00:31:13,404 --> 00:31:15,773
I never fail.

463
00:31:19,110 --> 00:31:22,714
Pulse 140. His right side is convulsing.

464
00:31:22,780 --> 00:31:24,983
- Fosphenytoin. 2 vials.
- Yes.

465
00:31:25,049 --> 00:31:27,685
Cool the brain surface. Give me saline.

466
00:31:28,186 --> 00:31:29,821
Don't kill the witness!

467
00:31:34,726 --> 00:31:35,560
Jonouchi.

468
00:31:37,595 --> 00:31:41,866
I thought about
what you can't buy with money.

469
00:31:43,935 --> 00:31:45,436
Not now.

470
00:31:45,503 --> 00:31:46,738
Dr. Daimon, saline.

471
00:31:54,579 --> 00:31:57,982
How about justice?

472
00:31:58,049 --> 00:31:58,983
Don't talk!

473
00:32:00,952 --> 00:32:05,823
February 13th, 2014...

474
00:32:07,158 --> 00:32:09,394
50 million yen to the Keimin Party.

475
00:32:10,695 --> 00:32:12,630
May 21st.

476
00:32:14,232 --> 00:32:17,669
The Kyusei Party's
Chief Secretary Miyajiri

477
00:32:18,870 --> 00:32:20,405
and Congressman Asakawa...

478
00:32:21,339 --> 00:32:22,707
30 million to each.

479
00:32:25,643 --> 00:32:26,878
September 7th.

480
00:32:28,513 --> 00:32:34,085
Minister Oizumi of the Ministry of
Health, Labour and Welfare... 50 million.

481
00:32:36,487 --> 00:32:40,058
I paid all that in cash.

482
00:32:43,061 --> 00:32:45,596
What has he done?

483
00:33:14,926 --> 00:33:18,396
One more thing.

484
00:33:21,599 --> 00:33:22,633
Jonouchi.

485
00:33:24,168 --> 00:33:25,370
Your secret...

486
00:33:27,138 --> 00:33:30,174
From senior year.

487
00:33:30,241 --> 00:33:31,709
Don't talk.

488
00:33:37,181 --> 00:33:38,449
What was that?

489
00:33:38,516 --> 00:33:40,752
Sir, we got a statement.

490
00:33:42,620 --> 00:33:45,456
You all just heard that statement, yes?

491
00:33:46,457 --> 00:33:47,291
Of course.

492
00:33:47,358 --> 00:33:49,427
No. I heard nothing.

493
00:33:53,631 --> 00:33:55,033
Pulse is stable.

494
00:33:56,000 --> 00:33:57,301
His convulsions stopped.

495
00:33:59,370 --> 00:34:00,505
Re-administer propofol.

496
00:34:00,571 --> 00:34:01,572
Yes.

497
00:34:04,008 --> 00:34:06,477
Place Carmustine.

498
00:34:06,544 --> 00:34:07,412
Yes.

499
00:34:08,880 --> 00:34:10,048
Carmustine?

500
00:34:11,149 --> 00:34:12,917
- The candy.
- Candy?

501
00:34:12,984 --> 00:34:14,218
Yeah, the candy.

502
00:34:15,686 --> 00:34:17,455
I see.

503
00:34:21,559 --> 00:34:24,729
Now I understand, Daimon.

504
00:34:25,797 --> 00:34:26,631
Carmustine.

505
00:34:40,278 --> 00:34:41,746
What is that?

506
00:34:41,813 --> 00:34:42,880
I'll explain.

507
00:34:43,481 --> 00:34:45,116
After removing the tumor,

508
00:34:45,183 --> 00:34:48,886
they placed the newest anticancer drug

509
00:34:48,953 --> 00:34:52,023
to inhibit growth
of remaining tumor cells.

510
00:34:52,824 --> 00:34:53,958
So he's fine?

511
00:34:54,025 --> 00:34:57,862
He will receive
chemo and radiation therapy.

512
00:34:57,929 --> 00:35:00,631
Then he can testify at trial?

513
00:35:00,698 --> 00:35:01,566
I believe so.

514
00:35:03,568 --> 00:35:05,069
It's truly Japan's best hospital.

515
00:35:05,770 --> 00:35:06,938
Thank you.

516
00:35:07,004 --> 00:35:09,073
I'm honored that we could help.

517
00:35:11,642 --> 00:35:12,577
It's all over.

518
00:35:14,112 --> 00:35:16,314
SURGERY TIME

519
00:35:17,248 --> 00:35:18,983
Glioblastoma resection

520
00:35:19,050 --> 00:35:20,952
and Carmustine placement complete.

521
00:35:21,285 --> 00:35:23,521
Blood loss 150. Blood pressure 100s.

522
00:35:23,588 --> 00:35:25,022
Pulse 60s and sinus.

523
00:35:34,465 --> 00:35:35,333
Thanks.

524
00:35:35,399 --> 00:35:36,901
Thank you.

525
00:35:38,936 --> 00:35:40,771
Good job.

526
00:35:43,508 --> 00:35:45,943
Bravo!

527
00:35:48,479 --> 00:35:51,516
No. Where are you going?

528
00:35:53,451 --> 00:35:54,285
Excuse me.

529
00:35:54,352 --> 00:35:55,853
Dr. Ebina!

530
00:35:55,920 --> 00:35:56,787
Yes, right away.

531
00:35:57,922 --> 00:35:59,590
Let me report.

532
00:35:59,657 --> 00:36:01,826
The operation was a success.

533
00:36:02,160 --> 00:36:04,195
Dr. Daimon did a fantastic job.

534
00:36:05,062 --> 00:36:06,531
Thank you.

535
00:36:06,597 --> 00:36:09,800
Also, the patient gave
a statement about a bribery.

536
00:36:14,705 --> 00:36:17,742
The Prosecutor's Office
thanked us for our work.

537
00:36:21,245 --> 00:36:23,147
Is that so...

538
00:36:23,214 --> 00:36:26,484
It was truly shocking.

539
00:36:27,151 --> 00:36:30,521
It seems that even Minister Oizumi
was receiving bribes.

540
00:36:32,924 --> 00:36:37,128
Thank you for your report.

541
00:36:37,195 --> 00:36:39,830
You're welcome. Excuse me.

542
00:36:46,437 --> 00:36:47,738
The Minister?

543
00:37:19,637 --> 00:37:23,207
I was wrong. It was the opposite.

544
00:37:38,189 --> 00:37:41,692
So I'm alive.

545
00:37:43,160 --> 00:37:45,796
But you're good as dead.

546
00:37:47,498 --> 00:37:48,633
You talked.

547
00:37:52,870 --> 00:37:55,306
I thought I was going to die.

548
00:37:58,676 --> 00:38:01,445
Michiko Daimon never fails...

549
00:38:05,516 --> 00:38:09,453
Regardless of what
sort of sin you've committed.

550
00:38:10,988 --> 00:38:14,025
Those who can only
atone for sins by dying...

551
00:38:14,825 --> 00:38:17,862
Those wishing to die from despair...

552
00:38:18,963 --> 00:38:20,398
Daimon saves those lives

553
00:38:21,265 --> 00:38:22,566
if they're in front of her.

554
00:38:23,601 --> 00:38:26,470
That's the kind of doctor she is.

555
00:38:30,041 --> 00:38:31,709
NATIONAL ADVANCED MEDICAL CENTER

556
00:38:31,776 --> 00:38:34,312
You say that I broke our promise...

557
00:38:35,012 --> 00:38:39,717
But justice for us doctors
is to save the patient's life.

558
00:38:40,418 --> 00:38:43,554
Justice? I'll be arrested.

559
00:38:43,621 --> 00:38:44,488
When that happens,

560
00:38:45,323 --> 00:38:47,925
I must scrap your plans for

561
00:38:47,992 --> 00:38:49,493
the Healthcare Organization.

562
00:38:50,161 --> 00:38:51,495
Do you understand?

563
00:38:52,029 --> 00:38:53,731
I don't think what you did

564
00:38:54,465 --> 00:38:58,402
will have any effect on
the Healthcare Organization.

565
00:39:01,238 --> 00:39:03,641
I'm sorry I couldn't be of any help.

566
00:39:05,776 --> 00:39:06,744
Goodbye.

567
00:39:10,815 --> 00:39:11,882
Mr. Tendo...

568
00:39:24,161 --> 00:39:25,296
Excuse me.

569
00:39:25,730 --> 00:39:28,999
Thank you for using

570
00:39:29,066 --> 00:39:30,434
our Daimon and Jonouchi.

571
00:39:34,872 --> 00:39:37,608
These are melons. This is a bill.

572
00:39:42,246 --> 00:39:46,150
As promised, I brought 2 melons.

573
00:39:47,885 --> 00:39:49,387
We don't need that.

574
00:39:49,453 --> 00:39:52,256
We will not pay this time.

575
00:39:56,527 --> 00:39:57,695
Excuse me.

576
00:39:58,496 --> 00:39:59,597
10 MILLION YEN

577
00:39:59,663 --> 00:40:02,299
I said we won't pay.

578
00:40:02,366 --> 00:40:05,002
What is this outrageous price?

579
00:40:05,069 --> 00:40:08,172
You were able to help the prosecution,

580
00:40:08,739 --> 00:40:14,779
and bring light to a dark suspicion
of the political world.

581
00:40:15,713 --> 00:40:17,681
You let justice prevail

582
00:40:18,215 --> 00:40:19,884
without being poisoned by evil.

583
00:40:21,285 --> 00:40:27,958
This was only possible with
Mr. Tendo's excellent judgment.

584
00:40:29,727 --> 00:40:34,298
I believe this hospital's character

585
00:40:34,832 --> 00:40:36,434
has become unquestionable.

586
00:40:43,307 --> 00:40:45,075
Very well.

587
00:40:47,445 --> 00:40:48,813
As usual...

588
00:40:50,514 --> 00:40:52,616
We will wire you the money.

589
00:40:52,683 --> 00:40:54,585
Thank you.

590
00:40:56,620 --> 00:40:58,989
It was a great operation.

591
00:41:02,726 --> 00:41:04,962
Please tell Dr. Daimon...

592
00:41:08,599 --> 00:41:11,702
That I'm extremely grateful.

593
00:41:28,152 --> 00:41:29,487
Please tell her.

594
00:41:35,092 --> 00:41:36,126
Yes,

595
00:41:37,294 --> 00:41:38,395
I will do so.

596
00:41:52,343 --> 00:41:53,844
How scary.

597
00:42:01,952 --> 00:42:04,889
KANBARA DOCTOR AGENCY

598
00:42:07,625 --> 00:42:09,693
Let's eat.

599
00:42:09,760 --> 00:42:11,595
Lend me 30,000 yen.

600
00:42:11,662 --> 00:42:14,064
I operated, so it's okay, right?

601
00:42:14,131 --> 00:42:15,566
You're in trouble.

602
00:42:15,633 --> 00:42:17,401
Mr. Tendo's mad.

603
00:42:17,468 --> 00:42:21,672
I'll be in trouble if I don't pay today.

604
00:42:21,739 --> 00:42:22,873
Pay?

605
00:42:27,811 --> 00:42:30,481
Look. I won 100 million yen.

606
00:42:31,415 --> 00:42:32,516
100 MILLION YEN

607
00:42:32,583 --> 00:42:37,087
If I deposit the 30,000 yen fee,
they'll give me 100 million yen.

608
00:42:37,154 --> 00:42:38,556
Yes!

609
00:42:38,622 --> 00:42:39,490
Michiko...

610
00:42:39,557 --> 00:42:40,391
Daimon...

611
00:42:41,258 --> 00:42:43,761
Of course you're shocked.

612
00:42:43,827 --> 00:42:45,896
I mean, it's 100 million.

613
00:42:45,963 --> 00:42:49,266
One, zero, zero, zero...

614
00:42:49,333 --> 00:42:51,335
You're being scammed.

615
00:42:51,402 --> 00:42:53,604
- That's fraud.
- Seriously?

616
00:42:53,671 --> 00:42:56,006
You really are dumb.

617
00:42:56,073 --> 00:42:57,808
Unbelievable. So dumb.

618
00:42:57,875 --> 00:42:59,710
- So dumb.
- Hold on.

619
00:43:00,611 --> 00:43:03,280
Are you sure you want to say that?

620
00:43:03,347 --> 00:43:04,481
What?

621
00:43:05,215 --> 00:43:09,153
Your unbelievable secret...

622
00:43:09,853 --> 00:43:13,490
Want me to say it?

623
00:43:13,557 --> 00:43:16,493
Wait. You know it?

624
00:43:16,894 --> 00:43:19,063
What do you mean "unbelievable"?

625
00:43:19,129 --> 00:43:20,197
Oh.

626
00:43:20,264 --> 00:43:21,799
- What!
- How dirty!

627
00:43:21,865 --> 00:43:23,701
- Wait!
- Oh no!

628
00:43:23,767 --> 00:43:25,135
Wait...

629
00:43:25,202 --> 00:43:26,503
What's so dirty?

630
00:43:27,605 --> 00:43:31,275
<i>She despises groups, authority</i>
<i>and institutional restraints.</i>

631
00:43:31,342 --> 00:43:35,145
<i>Her license and the skills she has earned</i>
<i>are her only weapons.</i>

632
00:43:35,212 --> 00:43:40,351
<i>To investigates the IT company bribery,</i>

633
00:43:40,417 --> 00:43:42,086
<i>the Prosecutor's Office has begun</i>

634
00:43:42,519 --> 00:43:47,191
<i>searching Minister Oizumi's office.</i>

635
00:43:47,758 --> 00:43:53,697
<i>It is thought that the Ministry's plans</i>

636
00:43:53,764 --> 00:43:58,569
<i>for the Japan Healthcare Organization</i>
<i>will be greatly set back due to this.</i>

637
00:43:58,636 --> 00:43:59,536
MEDICAL INDUSTRY CORRUPT?

638
00:44:35,005 --> 00:44:39,009
Michiko Daimon...
Be careful with that woman.

639
00:44:39,810 --> 00:44:43,814
She might become a cancer for you one day.

640
00:44:44,548 --> 00:44:47,384
But that toy is a double-edged sword.

641
00:44:47,451 --> 00:44:52,423
If you use it wrong, you'll be sliced.

642
00:45:08,238 --> 00:45:09,306
Scary.

643
00:45:26,557 --> 00:45:28,826
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

644
00:45:29,226 --> 00:45:30,194
<i>Also known as...</i>

645
00:45:30,894 --> 00:45:32,429
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

646
00:46:49,439 --> 00:46:51,942
We are in big trouble.

647
00:46:52,009 --> 00:46:54,812
That man. He loves groups and authority.

648
00:46:54,878 --> 00:46:56,113
Whose surgery is quicker?

649
00:46:56,180 --> 00:46:59,249
- We'll make it a race.
- I decline.

650
00:46:59,316 --> 00:47:01,985
Don't you have pride as a woman?

651
00:47:02,052 --> 00:47:03,420
I'll crush that woman.
